{"conversation_id":"ae995f44-d5a3-484c-82b4-695a353f4cd8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-23 04:02:04 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-23 11:02:04 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\nCoding-Agent: agy\nSession-ID: ae995f44-d5a3-484c-82b4-695a353f4cd8\n\nAppended the r3 review section to [1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/collab/yang-clojure/1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md).\n\n### r3 Review Summary (`7060af65`)\n\n1. **Handshake-order fix ([jvm.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj#L280-L345)):**\n   - Replaces the `ring.websocket.protocols/Listener` path (where http-kit sent `101 Switching Protocols` before invoking `on-open`, dropping any client frames arriving before `@adapter` was populated) with direct `AsyncChannel` upgrade handling in `upgrade!`.\n   - `upgrade!` runs `accept!` and registers `.setReceiveHandler` and `.setCloseRingHandler` on the `AsyncChannel` **before** `.sendHandshake` puts the `101` on the wire.\n   - `lifecycle` (`swap-vals!`) serializes pre- vs. post-handshake state: `:send!` refuses writes before `:open?` and returns `:dao.stream/closed` after `:close`; any early server close during `accept!` (rejection or exception) is recorded in `:close` and transmitted via `.serverClose` immediately after `.sendHandshake`, while post-handshake closes execute `.serverClose` directly once; `report-close!` is idempotent via `:reported?` and handles pre-registration channel disconnects (`(.isClosed channel)`).\n\n2. **Regression test ([jvm_test.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/test/dao/stream/ws/jvm_test.clj#L484-L526)):**\n   - `first-frame-can-arrive-before-endpoint-acknowledgement` deterministically gates `:accept!` on a promise, asserts that the client's handshake (`connecting`) blocks (`TimeoutException`) until `:accept!` finishes and the receive handler is installed, and verifies that a frame sent immediately from the client's `onOpen` callback (before `accept-and-ack-slot!` acknowledges the slot offer) is queued and received intact.\n\n3. **Scope \u0026 client compatibility:**\n   - Only [jvm.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj) and [jvm_test.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/test/dao/stream/ws/jvm_test.clj) are touched; no unrelated changes are present, and well-ordered clients see identical handshake headers, subprotocol negotiation, frame routing, and close behavior.\n\nVERDICT: CONFIRMED-CLOSED\n","duration_seconds":75373.784401,"num_turns":3,"usage":{"input_tokens":690063,"output_tokens":35737,"thinking_tokens":24347,"cache_read_tokens":3858008,"total_tokens":725800}}
